<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Tools on MCP Toolbox for Databases</title><link>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/</link><description>Recent content in Tools on MCP Toolbox for Databases</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>oracle-execute-sql</title><link>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/oracle-execute-sql/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/oracle-execute-sql/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="about"&gt;About&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;An &lt;code&gt;oracle-execute-sql&lt;/code&gt; tool executes a SQL statement against an Oracle&#10;database.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;oracle-execute-sql&lt;/code&gt; takes one input parameter &lt;code&gt;sql&lt;/code&gt; and runs the sql&#10;statement against the &lt;code&gt;source&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; This tool is intended for developer assistant workflows with&#10;human-in-the-loop and shouldn&amp;rsquo;t be used for production agents.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="compatible-sources"&gt;Compatible Sources&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="compatibility-section"&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;This tool can be used with the following database sources:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10; &lt;table&gt;&#10; &lt;thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;th&gt;Source Name&lt;/th&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;/thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tbody&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/source/"&gt;Oracle Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;/tbody&gt;&#10; &lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="example"&gt;Example&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-yaml" data-lang="yaml"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;kind&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;tool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;execute_sql_tool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;type&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;oracle-execute-sql&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;my-oracle-instance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nt"&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="l"&gt;Use this tool to execute sql statement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="w"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>oracle-list-tables</title><link>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/oracle-list-tables/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/oracle-list-tables/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="about"&gt;About&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;An &lt;code&gt;oracle-sql&lt;/code&gt; tool executes a pre-defined SQL statement against an&#10;Oracle database.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The specified SQL statement is executed using &lt;a href="https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/jdbc/basics/prepared.html"&gt;prepared statements&lt;/a&gt;&#10;for security and performance. It expects parameter placeholders in the SQL query&#10;to be in the native Oracle format (e.g., &lt;code&gt;:1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;:2&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;By default, tools are configured as &lt;strong&gt;read-only&lt;/strong&gt; (SAFE mode). To execute data modification&#10;statements (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE), you must explicitly set the &lt;code&gt;readOnly&lt;/code&gt;&#10;field to &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="compatible-sources"&gt;Compatible Sources&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="compatibility-section"&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;This tool can be used with the following database sources:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10; &lt;table&gt;&#10; &lt;thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;th&gt;Source Name&lt;/th&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;/thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tbody&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/source/"&gt;Oracle Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;/tbody&gt;&#10; &lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>oracle-sql</title><link>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/oracle-sql/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/tools/oracle-sql/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="about"&gt;About&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;An &lt;code&gt;oracle-sql&lt;/code&gt; tool executes a pre-defined SQL statement against an&#10;Oracle database.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The specified SQL statement is executed using &lt;a href="https://docs.oracle.com/javase/tutorial/jdbc/basics/prepared.html"&gt;prepared statements&lt;/a&gt;&#10;for security and performance. It expects parameter placeholders in the SQL query&#10;to be in the native Oracle format (e.g., &lt;code&gt;:1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;:2&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;By default, tools are configured as &lt;strong&gt;read-only&lt;/strong&gt; (SAFE mode). To execute data modification&#10;statements (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE), you must explicitly set the &lt;code&gt;readOnly&lt;/code&gt;&#10;field to &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="compatible-sources"&gt;Compatible Sources&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="compatibility-section"&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;This tool can be used with the following database sources:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10; &lt;table&gt;&#10; &lt;thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;th&gt;Source Name&lt;/th&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &lt;/thead&gt;&#10; &lt;tbody&gt;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;tr&gt;&#10; &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://mcp-toolbox.dev/v1.17.0/integrations/oracle/source/"&gt;Oracle Source&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10; &lt;/tr&gt;&#10; &#10;&#10; &#10;&#10; &#10; &#10; &lt;/tbody&gt;&#10; &lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>